db/ref 1069 "q-149711" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381118 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381118 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6y-x).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=6y-x,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381118 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c035203-351a-592d-b1dd-a7ea354f996d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381118 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=6y-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{6} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381119 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f5d8b9da-2e10-512b-a08c-50b084b89d21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921